cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Global Halal Compliance (GHC): A Cross-Domain Unified Protocol"
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite it as below.
  Once the v0.1 preprint is released, update with arXiv DOI.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The GHC Authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/khaaliswooden-max/ghc"
abstract: >-
  GHC is a cross-domain (food, pharma/cosmetics, Islamic finance,
  logistics) protocol for halal compliance grounded in category theory,
  information theory, quantum statistical mechanics, graph spectra, and
  zero-knowledge cryptography. The repository contains a machine-checked
  Lean 4 formalization, a Rust reference implementation, a protocol
  specification, and a peer-reviewable whitepaper.
keywords:
  - halal
  - supply chain
  - category theory
  - information theory
  - zero-knowledge proofs
  - traceability
  - Islamic finance
  - PROV-O
  - EPCIS
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-05-05"
